Fix the remaining Pod Metrics Snapshot UI issues. Keep a hard separation between Snapshot and Live Monitoring; do not modify or impact Live Monitoring.

1. Snapshot progress percentage
- Snapshot collection runs for the configured 15-second window.
- The progress animation must reach exactly 100% across the full 15 seconds.
- Currently it stops around 87% when the data arrives. Fix the progress calculation/timing so the animation reaches 100% for the full collection window.
- Do not artificially hold the animation after 100%.
- Keep the existing smooth animation.

2. Show loading state on every Snapshot run
- Every time the user clicks Run Metrics, replace the existing Snapshot results/table with the loading state.
- Do not keep displaying stale results while the new snapshot is being collected.
- This must work for repeated runs on the same application/namespace, not just the first run.
- Once the new snapshot completes, replace the loading state with the new results.

3. Add animated aggregation text
- Display "Loading Aggregate" above the progress bar while Snapshot aggregation is running.
- Animate the trailing dots sequentially:
  Loading Aggregate.
  Loading Aggregate..
  Loading Aggregate...
  then reset and repeat.
- Keep the existing progress bar and percentage unchanged apart from the timing fix.
- Use the existing dashboard styling; don't introduce unnecessary colors or additional UI.

4. Cancel/reset Snapshot UI when context changes
- If Snapshot collection is running and the user switches to a different application or namespace, immediately reset the Snapshot loading/collecting state for the previous context.
- The previous collection must not continue controlling the UI of the newly selected application/namespace.
- No loading animation, progress percentage, "Loading Aggregate..." state, or "Collecting" button state from the previous context should spill over into the newly selected context.
- If the newly selected application/namespace already has valid Snapshot data, show that data normally.
- If it has no data, show the normal empty state.
- Do not display data from the previous application/namespace.

5. Preserve existing behavior
- Do not change the Snapshot aggregation logic itself.
- Do not change the 15-second collection window or 5-sample/3-second sampling behavior.
- Do not modify Live Monitoring code or behavior.
- Inspect the existing implementation and relevant tests before changing anything.
- Update/add only the relevant tests for these fixes.
- Test repeated Snapshot runs.
- Test switching application during collection.
- Test switching namespace during collection.
- Test that the progress reaches 100% at the end of the 15-second window.
- Test the animated aggregation text/state.
- Run the relevant Pod Metrics test suite and Live Monitoring regression tests and fix any regression before completing.
